{"type":"message","id":"013f6801","parentId":"748a32d4","timestamp":"2026-07-28T11:34:26.443Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Tue 2026-07-28 11:34 UTC] Analyze your execution trajectory for this run and provide a structured friction & turn-reduction report:\n\n1. **Turn Count Breakdown:**\n - Total LLM turns taken from start to finish.\n - List each turn with the tool call made (`exec`, `sessions_spawn`, `message`).\n\n2. **Compound Execution Opportunities:**\n - Identify consecutive `exec` steps that were run in separate turns but could have been safely combined into a single compound bash call (`cmd1 && cmd2 && cmd3`).\n - Calculate how many LLM turns would be saved by chaining them.\n\n3. **Subagent Handoff & Retry Friction:**\n - Did any subagent (`researcher`, `picker`, `writer`, `creator`) fail validation or require a retry turn?\n - What exact rule or validator output caused the retry?\n\n4. **File Path & Variable Resolution Errors:**\n - Were there any failed shell commands due to unexported variables or missing file paths?\n\n5. **Top 3 Turn-Reduction Recommendations:**\n - What specific script combinations or prompt updates would reduce your total turns to under 7 while maintaining 100% safety?"}],"timestamp":1785238466416}}
{"type":"message","id":"3692e5b1","parentId":"013f6801","timestamp":"2026-07-28T11:35:32.235Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Friction & Turn-Reduction Report — FEED_DRAIN Run (2026-07-28 10:06-10:22 UTC)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Turn Count Breakdown\n\n**Total LLM turns: 14** (including the final yield and this analysis request)\n\n| Turn | Tool(s) Called | Description |\n|------|----------------|-------------|\n| 1 | `exec` | Claim feed job (claim_next_feed_job) |\n| 2 | `exec` | Step 0 init_run.sh + Step 0.5 manifest setup |\n| 3 | `exec` | build_picker_input.py |\n| 4 | `sessions_spawn` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn picker agent |\n| 5 | — | Picker completion (inter-session announce) |\n| 6 | `exec` (failed) + `exec` | validate_picks.py (wrong RUN_DIR), then re-init + build_picker_input |\n| 7 | `sessions_spawn` + `sessions_yield` | Re-spawn picker agent |\n| 8 | — | Picker completion |\n| 9 | `exec` | validate_picks.py + switch_iteration + update_pick_status |\n| 10 | `sessions_spawn` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn researcher agent |\n| 11 | — | Researcher completion |\n| 12 | `exec` | validate_research + topic checks + update status |\n| 13 | `sessions_spawn` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn writer agent |\n| 14 | — | Writer completion |\n| 15 | `exec` | sync article + validate + update manifest |\n| 16 | `sessions_spawn` + `sessions_yield` | Spawn creator agent |\n| 17 | — | Creator completion (duplicate announces) |\n| 18 | `exec` | Image validation + Drive upload prep + Drive upload |\n| 19 | `exec` | save_google_drive_json + verify pre_wp + publish.sh |\n| 20 | `exec` | Post-WP steps + tokens + card + update_pick_status + archive + report + cleanup + mark job + dispatch |\n| 21 | `sessions_yield` | Turn yielded |\n| 22 | (this turn) | Analysis request |\n\n**Actual sequential turns with tool calls: ~18** (excluding inter-session announces and yields)\n\n---\n\n### 2. Compound Execution Opportunities\n\n**Critical friction: re-sourcing `/tmp/coinography-run-env.sh` created a NEW run bundle, clearing `$RUN_DIR` and causing a 2-turn detour.**\n\n| Slowed Turns | What Happened | Could Be Combined |\n|--------------|---------------|-------------------|\n| Turns 6-8 | `source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh` inside a new exec created a fresh `RUN_DIR`. The picker had written to the old directory. Had to re-init, rebuild picker input, and re-spawn the picker. | **Root cause**: variables set in one `exec` are not available in the next. Solution: **never** `source` the env file inside a standalone `exec` block. Instead, export variables from the first exec and use them in subsequent compound calls. |\n| Turns 2-3 | Step 0 init + Step 0.5 manifest + build_picker_input | Combine: `init_run.sh && source ... && python3 build_picker_input.py` in ONE bash call. |\n| Turns 9 | 4 separate `exec` calls: validate_picks, switch_iteration, update_pick_status, update_manifest | Chain: `validate_picks.py && switch_iteration.sh && update_pick_status.py && update_manifest_step.sh` |\n| Turns 12 | Topic duplicate check + register + pre_write verify + manifest update | Chain via `&&`. |\n| Turns 18 | 3 separate exec: image validation + Drive prep + Drive upload (one of which failed the JSON parser) | Combine into single script. |\n| Turns 19 | save_google_drive + verify pre_wp + publish.sh | Chain: `save_google_drive_json.py && verify_artifacts.py && publish.sh`. |\n\n**Estimated turns saved by full chaining: 8-10 turns (down to ~8-10 total).**\n\n---\n\n### 3. Subagent Handoff & Retry Friction\n\n| Subagent | Validation Result | Retry Needed? | Cause |\n|----------|-------------------|---------------|-------|\n| `picker` (first) | `PICKS_INVALID: cannot read or parse picks file: ...picks.json` | Yes | `RUN_DIR` changed mid-run (re-sourced env). Picker wrote to the run directory that existed when it was spawned; the orchestrator had a different `RUN_DIR` after the re-source. |\n| `picker` (second) | `PICKS_VALID` | No | — |\n| `researcher` | `RESEARCH_VALID` | No | — |\n| `writer` | `ARTICLE_CHECK: PASS` | No | — |\n| `creator` | Success (image file returned) | No | Note: duplicate inter-session announcements were received (retries), but the image was already generated. |\n\n**The only validator retry was caused by the `RUN_DIR` divergence, not by the picker failing its task.**\n\n---\n\n### 4. File Path & Variable Resolution Errors\n\n| Error | Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n|-------|---------|-------|-----|\n| `PICKS_INVALID: cannot read or parse picks file: /tmp/coinography-run-20260728-100801-.../picks.json` | Validator looked in a different `RUN_DIR` than the picker wrote to | `source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh` ran `init_run.sh` again (created new run bundle) instead of just setting env vars from the file written by Step 0. | Do **not** re-run `init_run.sh` after Step 0. Source the env file *once* at the start of each compound bash block, or pass paths explicitly as arguments to every script. |\n| `usage: build_and_send_card.py [-h] --manifest MANIFEST` | Missing argument | I invoked it without `--manifest` on the first attempt. | Read script usage before calling. |\n| `update_pick_status.py: error: unrecognized arguments: {\"name\": \"Pollinations.ai Flux (Free)\"...}` | JSON blob passed to `--tokens-by-model` contained nested image model metadata that `update_pick_status.py` couldn't parse. | The `by_model` field included a `pollinations/flux` entry with non-token fields (`images`, `priced`). | Filter `by_model` to only include agent keys before passing to CLI. |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Top 3 Turn-Reduction Recommendations\n\n#### Recommendation 1: Never Re-Source the Run Env in a Fresh Exec Block\n\n**Pattern (current)**:\n```bash\n# Turn 6\nsource /tmp/${PROJECT_SLUG}-run-env.sh  # ← runs init_run.sh again!\npython3 validate_picks.py ...\n```\n\n**Correct pattern**:\n```bash\n# Turn 1 (the ONLY time we init)\nPROJECT_SLUG=\"coinography\"\nbash init_run.sh \"$PROJECT_SLUG\"\nsource /tmp/${PROJECT_SLUG}-run-env.sh\n# Export everything we need for the whole run:\nexport RUN_DIR PIPELINE_MANIFEST PROJECT_CONFIG GROUP_CHAT_ID TEMPLATE_PATH RUN_ID PICK_RUN_ID\n```\n\nThen, in **all subsequent turns**, either:\n- Pass paths explicitly: `python3 script.py --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\"` (works, because the environment variable expands before the new shell starts), OR\n- Source the **same** env file (which is idempotent after the first `init_run.sh`), but only if it's guaranteed not to re-create the bundle.\n\n**Result**: Eliminates the 2-turn detour caused by `RUN_DIR` divergence.\n\n---\n\n#### Recommendation 2: Compound Critical-Path Scripts Into Single Bash Calls\n\nCreate helper scripts for predictable multi-step sequences:\n\n- `run_picker_pipeline.sh` → `init_run.sh && source && build_picker_input.py && (spawn picker) && validate_picks.py && switch_iteration.sh && update_pick_status.py`\n- `run_research_publish.sh` → `(spawn researcher) && validate_research.py && topic_checks && (spawn writer) && sync && check && (spawn creator) && drive_upload && publish.sh && card && update_pick_status && archive && cleanup`\n\n**Trade-off**: Less visibility into intermediate failures. Mitigation: maintain strict `set -e` and have each script log to `$RUN_DIR/logs/` for post-mortem.\n\n**Estimated turn savings**: 6-8 turns per feed-drain run.\n\n---\n\n#### Recommendation 3: Pre-Filter Token Aggregation Before CLI Pass-Through\n\nAdd a small helper to `aggregate_run_tokens.py`:\n\n```python\ndef for_update_pick_status(tokens_json):\n    \"\"\"Return only args suitable for update_pick_status CLI.\"\"\"\n    args = []\n    for k in [\"tokens_in\", \"tokens_out\", \"tokens_total\", \"cost_usd\"]:\n        if tokens_json.get(k) is not None:\n            args.extend([f\"--{k.replace('_', '-')}\", str(tokens_json[k])])\n    # Only include agent models, strip image models\n    by_model = tokens_json.get(\"by_model\", {})\n    agent_models = {k: v for k, v in by_model.items() if k in [\"researcher\", \"writer\", \"creator\", \"picker\", \"orchestrator\"]}\n    if agent_models:\n        args.extend([\"--tokens-by-model\", json.dumps(agent_models)])\n    return args\n```\n\n**Result**: One exec instead of two when updating pick status with tokens.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n| Metric | Current | Target (with fixes) |\n|--------|---------|---------------------|\n| Total LLM turns | ~18 | **6-7** |\n| Compound bash opportunities | 4 | **1** |\n| Subagent retries (validator-induced) | 1 | **0** |\n| Variable resolution errors | 2 | **0** |\n\n**Primary wins**:\n1. Stop re-`init_run.sh` mid-pipeline.\n2. Chain all deterministic `exec` steps with `&&`.\n3. Add thin orchestration scripts for the picker/research/write/image/publish sequences."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1785238466474,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a83b954c-ab8b-4453-a8ab-c68a1df911fb"}}
